{"ts":"2026-05-29T00:25:48.699Z","author":"maintainer-agent","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Reorder classifyItem so BUG_LIKE_ITEM_TYPES default-Fixed runs before the weak change/update/refactor/improve keyword bucket, after the explicit security/removed/fix/feature checks."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pmc-874d"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Classifier misroutes Issues with CLI command-name titles (update/change) to Changed not Fixed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The keyword classifier scans [type, tags, title] and matches the Changed needle 'update'/'updated' against CLI command names like 'pm update' in Issue titles. pm-cli's Issue 'pm update doesn't accept --expected/--actual aliases that pm close accepts' was filed under Changed solely because its title contains the command word 'update'. Same class of defect as #19 (CLI flag tokens leaking into Added). Fix: let a bug-like item TYPE (issue/bug/bugfix/defect) win over the weak Changed keywords (update/change/refactor/improve), keeping explicit security/removed/fix/feature signals ahead; non-bug types (task/chore) still route 'update dependency ...' to Changed."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["bug","classifier"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-05-29T00:25:48.699Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-05-29T00:25:48.699Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/deadline","value":"2026-05-30T00:00:00.000Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/assignee","value":"maintainer-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"maintainer-agent"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":30},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Issue/Bug/Defect titled with command words update/change route to Fixed; chore 'update dependency' stays Changed; explicit feature tag still wins; regression tests added; dist rebuilt; changelog:check passes"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reviewer","value":"steve"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pmc-2lzr","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-05-29T00:25:48.699Z","author":"maintainer-agent"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-05-29T00:25:48.699Z","author":"maintainer-agent","text":"Discovered while shipping pm-cli pm-1lws which was misfiled under Changed"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes","value":[{"created_at":"2026-05-29T00:25:48.699Z","author":"maintainer-agent","text":"Same command-name-collision class as the #19 CLI-flag-token fix"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings","value":[{"created_at":"2026-05-29T00:25:48.699Z","author":"maintainer-agent","text":"Item TYPE is a stronger classification signal than ambiguous title keywords that collide with command/flag names"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/files","value":[{"path":"src/generator.ts","scope":"project","note":"classifier reorder"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tests","value":[{"command":"npm test","scope":"project","timeout_seconds":240}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/docs","value":[{"path":"src/generator.ts","scope":"project","note":"classifyItem ordering"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"bc248c4390aeebd4bc7d7ea94d9667fdd6f5be381ed5fc629f3d60daf547be09","message":"File classifier command-name collision issue"}
